s relations between Washington and Kyiv deteriorate.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>At least four dead after flooding in eastern Spain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a6dd0e9c19ef5bc741e420b833436cae1ea2bafba0a0e8c717794abc3aeb50c</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:02:54Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T00:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/at-least-four-dead-after-flooding-in-eastern-spain/a-79707781--614c93a32fdc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/at-least-four-dead-after-flooding-in-eastern-spain/a-79707781?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At least four people have died in Spain as torrential rain has battered the country's eastern Mediterranean coast. The severe flooding had left more than 450 people stranded on rooftops, in buildings or in cars.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>French authorities impose partial curfews in Paris, Nice</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:070d4723647b148e30e90d02ef92e806505f5df695e2d723b8f206c3fdc6eeeb</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:02:57Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T19:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/french-authorities-impose-partial-curfews-in-paris-nice/live-79707186--e0380865f87c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/french-authorities-impose-partial-curfews-in-paris-nice/live-79707186?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">French authorities imposed curfews in towns and cities on Monday night after cost-of-living and anti-government protests descended into rioting and looting over the weekend. DW has the latest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bulgaria seeks suspects in Germany after Starlink sabotage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0130fc93d4ffc3b8011275af658abd1a4cb9e46c3d17f553c7a04bf048ae6856</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T18:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-seeks-suspects-in-germany-after-starlink-sabotage/a-79706745--e11bc2352fd6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-seeks-suspects-in-germany-after-starlink-sabotage/a-79706745?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Bulgarian court has issued arrest warrants for two young German nationals suspected of setting fire to Starlink antennas. The case is reminiscent of another in Poland, which Warsaw says was orchestrated by Russia.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Emergency at Leipzig airport sparked by novice driver</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:970c51ca0e5271f35bcb07ffdd218347cc9bd5ae69b16a85bb369d00cd3f88ac</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T17:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-emergency-at-leipzig-airport-sparked-by-novice-driver/live-79695354--1d0844a30c8b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-emergency-at-leipzig-airport-sparked-by-novice-driver/live-79695354?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two men breached a fence at the Leipzig/Halle airport while practicing for a driving test. Meanwhile, German Chancellor Friedrich Merz announced an industrial AI partnership with Nvidia. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Kenya: Cult leader guilty of murdering 190 children, 1 adult</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8dd7bafc33417b4ffb18f7dc50e801642f34055bfe5e625a8fb9d966f1486f5c</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T15:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kenya-cult-leader-guilty-of-murdering-190-children-1-adult/a-79706279--f2f58ea97f8b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kenya-cult-leader-guilty-of-murdering-190-children-1-adult/a-79706279?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Preacher Paul Mackenzie was accused of encouraging his followers to starve themselves to death. He ran a Christian doomsday cult called the Good News International Church that claimed the end of the world was imminent.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Canada: Alberta votes on holding independence referendum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a194627ad36ab8431ec3113af9526bf1f6e1dedc3304eefa543891bc3469ecc</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T15:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/canada-alberta-votes-on-holding-independence-referendum/a-79700283--4cfaa44e1aaa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/canada-alberta-votes-on-holding-independence-referendum/a-79700283?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Canada's oil-rich western province of Alberta is not deemed likely to vote in favor of a real breakaway plebiscite. Nevertheless the separatist movement hopes to gain leverage over Mark Carney's government.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Can diplomacy stop another Ethiopia-Eritrea war?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e45144f8e4824037f75a4e63d7fdaefeafc34cfc7c8c7ff95078bee622d6e6d9</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T15:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-diplomacy-stop-another-ethiopia-eritrea-war/a-79705435--b90ab4301994.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-diplomacy-stop-another-ethiopia-eritrea-war/a-79705435?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ethiopia has installed a new administration in conflict-hit Tigray after federal forces pushed back Tigrayan fighters. But tensions with Eritrea continue to raise fears of a wider regional war.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Houthi strike on Yemen government military camp kills at least 50</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b09c0507b00e48bfc706e5a57137b12c328851eff25cac21552dae66d46cdc9e</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T14:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/houthi-strike-on-yemen-government-military-camp-kills-at-least-50/a-79702163--d01e5a08fc37.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/houthi-strike-on-yemen-government-military-camp-kills-at-least-50/a-79702163?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Iran-backed group has claimed responsibility for the attack which killed new recruits at a military camp. The strikes follow deadly attacks over the weekend blamed on Saudi-led forces.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Rubio visits India with a trip to the world's largest oil refinery topping the agenda</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da9ef21fc86066b0845a443b7f7573740d47ccee55d993371749e914ee8e8d0e</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/rubio-visits-india-with-a-trip-to-the-world-s-largest-oil-refinery-topping-the-agenda/a-79699826--dd280f73407c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/rubio-visits-india-with-a-trip-to-the-world-s-largest-oil-refinery-topping-the-agenda/a-79699826?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A visit to India this week by Washington's top diplomat will skip New Delhi and instead include the world's largest oil refinery, which processes massive amounts of Russian crude. Is Trump looking for a new deal?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Myanmar refugees find hope in Thailand's work program</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d13298770c00d2bae3f1dc16a75f357515a0e9eb9d4035d90ef6409120d273bd</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/myanmar-refugees-find-hope-in-thailand-s-work-program/a-79697921--572ae4634b5b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/myanmar-refugees-find-hope-in-thailand-s-work-program/a-79697921?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A year ago, Thailand granted long-staying refugees from Myanmar the right to work legally. Refugees and rights groups welcome the move but say the program's first year has exposed significant shortcomings.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>UN food program cuts aid to 500,000 Palestinians in Gaza</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2aebf428c42851cc57712436323eea2c3f42692c0cb6fe969058d1eb4f252ac3</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T11:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/un-food-program-cuts-aid-to-500-000-palestinians-in-gaza/a-79699408--5a5f72f6f26c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/un-food-program-cuts-aid-to-500-000-palestinians-in-gaza/a-79699408?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Amid funding shortages, the World Food Program has said it is being forced to reduce necessary aid. Over two-thirds of Palestinians in Gaza are facing acute hunger, according to the agency.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>From delivery driver to global fame: A Korean writer's journey</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:45609c24e9502642d688b35e23e8d7525d714be6fd3a1e14a8102b1669275fcb</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T10:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/from-delivery-driver-to-global-fame-a-korean-writer-s-journey/a-79672757--a579002c20b4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/from-delivery-driver-to-global-fame-a-korean-writer-s-journey/a-79672757?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">You Yeong-Gwang's The Rainfall Market tells the story of a mysterious, hidden shop that only opens when it rains. For a debut novel by an unknown author, it was a massive success.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>The homeless man living in front of a London mega-mansion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18d4e91f94f8de15768939daf2f3b0d8282f5dd06a285d71c3638f73791d6716</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T10:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-homeless-man-living-in-front-of-a-london-mega-mansion/a-79400925--903398310f06.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-homeless-man-living-in-front-of-a-london-mega-mansion/a-79400925?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Anders Fernstedt lives in London without any money. The Swedish native has built a most unusual home under the porch of a house worth over €200 million. How did that happen?</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Greece: At least 12 die in migrant drownings overnight</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:899135872e1f71a774e0dd1cc3781cdc07e54d62dc62aaa7bc876bf23f853c09</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T10:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/greece-at-least-12-die-in-migrant-drownings-overnight/a-79697504--c57fcdcb2d55.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/greece-at-least-12-die-in-migrant-drownings-overnight/a-79697504?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Authorities say 12 people, including an infant, have drowned in Greek waters in two separate incidents overnight. Another 22 people were rescued. A search-and-rescue operation is ongoing.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Australian MP seriously hurt in suspected car attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:615c24a3e5a6670b61922209687816dd9ce21511b136d09270c9bcc0cb9542ed</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T10:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/australian-mp-seriously-hurt-in-suspected-car-attack/a-79697660--8ec3224c2b82.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/australian-mp-seriously-hurt-in-suspected-car-attack/a-79697660?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Helen Haines, an independent federal lawmaker, has been struck by a car in what Australia's prime minister has called an apparent attack.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine got 'no warning' of Russian ballistic strikes, Zelenskyy says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c79e10aa63f576f1c7d77a9372f0ceaa2652b77356143abf5c5b5ada8154e36e</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T10:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-got-no-warning-of-russian-ballistic-strikes-zelenskyy-says/a-79697476--5920f765895a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-got-no-warning-of-russian-ballistic-strikes-zelenskyy-says/a-79697476?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Massive strikes overnight hit the capital Kyiv, and damaged power stations, killing at least one person and cutting power to hundreds of thousands.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>West Bank: Israel arrests 10 suspects over settler attacks on US journalist, European diplomats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b13d7483262f377a14974d13f6a40f94d9093bf2d689aad888064a45986f5ad5</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T08:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/west-bank-israel-arrests-10-suspects-over-settler-attacks-on-us-journalist-european-diplomats/a-79696514--0a48dd473819.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/west-bank-israel-arrests-10-suspects-over-settler-attacks-on-us-journalist-european-diplomats/a-79696514?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Israeli police made the arrests following attacks on a US journalist and European diplomats in the occupied West Bank. Israeli human rights group Yesh Din has reported at least 170 settler attacks since September 27.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Deepfakes, bots and distrust: How AI is shaping Israel's election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bf3d4d6bc57a9a7e68e95ee1f8914b77fb3baa17fda8b8dbd1bfbf5ceeb1a0ef</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T08:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/deepfakes-bots-and-distrust-how-ai-is-shaping-israel-s-election/a-79657988--dfb913004f7f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/deepfakes-bots-and-distrust-how-ai-is-shaping-israel-s-election/a-79657988?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For the first time, AI is playing a major role in Israel's elections. Observers warn that deepfakes, bots and influence campaigns could sway voters.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India news: CJP alleges 'deliberate' delay in leaders' release</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:626870e9332383017de15e2562374e79bfc423c1dafe7507a8de63344d621ea3</id><updated>2026-10-20T05:01:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T06:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-cjp-alleges-deliberate-delay-in-leaders-release/live-79695410--74850181e334.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-cjp-alleges-deliberate-delay-in-leaders-release/live-79695410?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">CJP leaders Saurav Das and Ashutosh Ranka were due to be released on Sunday. The judge in the case has recused himself after claiming that he was threatened.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
